Binary search
=============

Part of CACHE_FRAMEWORK: the same kernels as A653_Benchmarks, kept as a
separate set for cache studies (cache locking and cache-miss analysis). The
algorithm is identical to A653_Benchmarks/BinSearch unless noted below.

What it tests
-------------

Execution time of a binary search: short, branch-heavy code with data-dependent
control flow.

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with one periodic process.

Searches a key in a sorted table of 15 (key, value) records, halving the range
at each step. Period and time capacity: 100 ms.

Expected output
---------------

Trace of the search steps (MID-1, MID+1, FOUND!!) every period.

Origin
------

Ported from SNU-RT benchmark suite (Seoul National University real-time
benchmarks).

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/BinSearch/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/BinSearch/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
